    'MMR vaccines are grown in chick embryo fibroblast cultures and contain negligible amounts of egg protein; egg-allergic children, even with anaphylaxis to egg, can safely receive MMR in the usual way (most guidelines advise routine settings, with standard anaphylaxis preparedness). Reactions to MMR are more likely due to gelatin or neomycin. Influenza vaccines (egg-based) are also considered safe in egg allergy. True contraindications to MMR include previous anaphylaxis to the vaccine or its components, severe immunosuppression and pregnancy.',
